Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:41:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] multitenant: add cmd/spike binary and Phase 2 findings
 doc

cmd/spike exercises the Manager against 5 distinct tenants and reports
cold-start latency, steady-state heap delta, LRU eviction at MaxActive=3,
VK resolver overhead (cached vs uncached), and shutdown drain time.

Measured on this hardware with tuned settings (Concurrency=4, Buffer=16,
InitialPoolSize=32, no MCP, no plugins):

  cold-start Acquire-to-Init   25-65 us
  per-tenant heap (avg of 3)   ~10 KiB
  per-tenant goroutines        5
  LRU eviction + new Acquire   ~50 us
  cached VK resolve            42 ns/op
  Manager.Shutdown (3 tenants) 20 us

SPIKE_FINDINGS.md documents what's proven, what's still unmeasured
(plugin footprint, MCP subprocess cost), and the recommended next steps
before committing to Phase 1 (DB schema).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
